{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0034", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "3 - Applying Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Central to most response plans will be the application of the mitigations described later in this document.", "paraphrase": "Most response plans center on applying mitigations described later in the document.", "modal_register": "mandatory", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0035", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "3 - Applying Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "For misuse, we have two categories of mitigations: security mitigations intended to prevent the exfiltration of model weights, and deployment mitigations (such as safety fine-tuning and misuse filtering, detection, and response) intended to counter the misuse of critical capabilities in deployments.", "paraphrase": "Misuse mitigations fall into two categories: security mitigations against weight exfiltration, and deployment mitigations against deployment misuse.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0036", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "3 - Applying Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "For deceptive alignment risk, automated monitoring may be applied to detect and respond to deceptive behavior for models that meet the first deceptive alignment CCL.", "paraphrase": "For deceptive alignment risk, automated monitoring may be used to detect and respond to deceptive behavior at the first CCL.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0037", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "3 - Applying Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Note that these mitigations reflect considerations from the perspective of addressing severe risks from powerful capabilities alone; due to this focused scope, other risk management and security considerations may result in more stringent mitigations applied to a model than specified by the Framework.", "paraphrase": "These mitigations only address severe-risk considerations, and other risk factors may lead to stricter mitigations than the Framework specifies.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0038", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "3 - Applying Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "A model flagged by an alert threshold may be assessed to pose risks for which readily available mitigations (including but not limited to those described below) may not be sufficient.", "paraphrase": "A flagged model may pose risks that available mitigations cannot sufficiently address.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0039", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "3 - Applying Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "If this happens, the response plan may involve putting deployment or further development on hold until adequate mitigations can be applied.", "paraphrase": "In that case, the response plan may pause deployment or development until adequate mitigations exist.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0040", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "3 - Applying Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Conversely, where model capabilities remain quite distant from a CCL, a response plan may involve the adoption of additional capability assessment processes to flag when heightened mitigations may be required.", "paraphrase": "Where capabilities are far from a CCL, the response plan may add capability assessment processes to flag future needs for heightened mitigations.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0041", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "3 - Applying Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "The appropriateness and efficacy of applied mitigations should be reviewed periodically, drawing on information like related misuse or misuse attempt incidents; results from continued post-mitigation testing; statistics about our intelligence, monitoring and escalation processes; and updated threat modeling and risk landscape analysis.", "paraphrase": "Applied mitigations should be periodically reviewed using incident data, post-mitigation testing, monitoring statistics, and updated threat modeling.", "modal_register": "mandatory", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0042", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Misuse", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "This section describes our mitigation approach for models that pose risks of severe harm through misuse, and then details our set of misuse CCLs, as well as the mitigations that we provisionally assess as appropriate for them.", "paraphrase": "This section outlines the mitigation approach, misuse CCLs, and provisional appropriate mitigations.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0043", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Mitigation Approach", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "There are two categories of mitigations to address models with misuse critical capabilities: security mitigations intended to prevent the exfiltration of model weights, and deployment mitigations intended to counter the misuse of critical capabilities in deployments.", "paraphrase": "There are two mitigation categories: security mitigations against exfiltration and deployment mitigations against misuse in deployment.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0035", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0044", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Mitigation Approach", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "For security, we have several levels of mitigations, allowing calibration of the robustness of security measures to the risks posed.", "paraphrase": "Security mitigations have multiple levels to calibrate robustness to risk.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0045", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Mitigation Approach", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "For deployment mitigations, we specify a standard process for applying, assessing, and reviewing mitigations: the aim of this process is to calibrate mitigations to CCLs, and the procedural approach reflects the more iterative and CCL-dependent nature of deployment mitigations.", "paraphrase": "A standard process for applying, assessing and reviewing deployment mitigations calibrates them iteratively to CCLs.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0046", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Security mitigations against exfiltration risk are important for models reaching CCLs.", "paraphrase": "Security mitigations against exfiltration are important for models that reach CCLs.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0047", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "This is because the release of model weights may enable the removal of any safeguards trained into or deployed with the model, and hence access (including by threat actors) to any critical capabilities.", "paraphrase": "Releasing model weights could allow removal of safeguards and grant threat actors access to critical capabilities.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0048", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Here, we rely on the RAND framework to articulate the level of security recommended for each CCL.", "paraphrase": "Google uses the RAND framework to specify recommended security levels per CCL.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0049", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "When we reference RAND security levels, we are referring to the security principles in their framework, rather than the benchmarks (i.e. concrete measures) also described in the RAND report.", "paraphrase": "References to RAND security levels refer to the underlying principles, not the concrete benchmarks in the RAND report.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0050", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Because AI security is an area of active research, we expect the concrete measures implemented to reach each level of security to evolve substantially.", "paraphrase": "Since AI security is an active research area, the concrete measures for each security level are expected to evolve significantly.", "modal_register": "aspirational", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0051", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Deployment Mitigations", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "The following deployment mitigation process will be applied to models reaching a CCL, allowing for iterative and flexible tailoring of mitigations to each risk and use case.", "paraphrase": "A deployment mitigation process will apply to models reaching a CCL, allowing iterative, tailored mitigations.", "modal_register": "mandatory", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0052", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Deployment Mitigations", "locator": "numbered 1", "unit_type": "numbered", "context_stem": "The following deployment mitigation process will be applied to models reaching a CCL.", "excerpt": "Development and assessment of mitigations: safeguards and an accompanying safety case are developed by iterating on the following:", "paraphrase": "Step 1 involves iteratively developing safeguards and a corresponding safety case.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0053", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Deployment Mitigations", "locator": "numbered 1 / sub a", "unit_type": "numbered", "context_stem": "Development and assessment of mitigations: safeguards and an accompanying safety case are developed by iterating on the following:", "excerpt": "Developing and improving a suite of safeguards targeting the capability. This includes, as appropriate, safety fine-tuning, misuse filtering and detection, and response protocols.", "paraphrase": "Sub-step a is developing and improving safeguards, including safety fine-tuning, misuse filtering/detection, and response protocols.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0054", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Deployment Mitigations", "locator": "numbered 1 / sub b", "unit_type": "numbered", "context_stem": "Development and assessment of mitigations: safeguards and an accompanying safety case are developed by iterating on the following:", "excerpt": "Assessing the robustness of these mitigations against the risk posed through assurance evaluations and threat modeling research. The assessment takes the form of a safety case, taking into account factors such as the likelihood and consequences of misuse.", "paraphrase": "Sub-step b is assessing mitigation robustness via assurance evaluations and threat modeling, producing a safety case that weighs likelihood and consequences of misuse.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0055", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Deployment Mitigations", "locator": "numbered 2", "unit_type": "numbered", "context_stem": "The following deployment mitigation process will be applied to models reaching a CCL.", "excerpt": "Pre-deployment review of safety case: general availability deployment of a model takes place only after the appropriate corporate governance body determines the safety case regarding each CCL the model has reached to be adequate.", "paraphrase": "Step 2 requires that general availability deployment occur only after a governance body approves the safety case for each reached CCL.", "modal_register": "mandatory", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0056", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Deployment Mitigations", "locator": "numbered 3", "unit_type": "numbered", "context_stem": "The following deployment mitigation process will be applied to models reaching a CCL.", "excerpt": "Post-deployment review of safety case: the safety case will be updated through red-teaming and revisions to our threat models. The safeguards for the model may be updated as well to ensure continued adequacy.", "paraphrase": "Step 3 updates the safety case through red-teaming and revised threat models, potentially updating safeguards to maintain adequacy.", "modal_register": "mandatory", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0057", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Misuse Critical Capability Levels", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "The table below details a set of CCLs we have identified through ongoing analysis of the CBRN, Cyber, and Machine Learning R&D risk domains.", "paraphrase": "A table lists CCLs identified through ongoing analysis across CBRN, Cyber, and ML R&D domains.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0058", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Misuse Critical Capability Levels", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "We expect these to evolve over time.", "paraphrase": "The CCLs are expected to change over time.", "modal_register": "aspirational", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0059", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Misuse Critical Capability Levels", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "We recommend a security level to each of these CCLs, which reflect our assessment of the minimum appropriate level of security the field of frontier AI should apply to models reaching each CCL.", "paraphrase": "A recommended security level is given per CCL, reflecting the assessed minimum appropriate security for the field.", "modal_register": "aspirational", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0060", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Misuse Critical Capability Levels", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "In practice, our overall security posture may commonly exceed the baseline levels recommended here.", "paraphrase": "Google's actual security posture may often exceed the recommended baseline levels.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0061", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Misuse Critical Capability Levels", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "These recommended security levels reflect our current thinking and may be adjusted if our empirical understanding of the risks changes.", "paraphrase": "The recommended security levels may change as empirical understanding of the risks evolves.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0062", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Misuse Critical Capability Levels", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "This may occur if, for example, a model does not possess capabilities meaningfully different from other widely available models that have not demonstrably caused or contributed to severe risks, or if we assess that the benefits of the open release of model weights outweigh the risks.", "paraphrase": "Adjustment may occur if a model's capabilities are not meaningfully different from other safe, widely available models, or if open release benefits are judged to outweigh risks.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0063", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Misuse Critical Capability Levels", "locator": "N/A", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Relatedly, we believe these recommendations will only be effective if the entire frontier AI field applies them, and of limited social utility if not.", "paraphrase": "The recommendations are believed to be effective only with field-wide adoption, otherwise of limited social value.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0064", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn4", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "See https://www.rand.org/pubs/research_reports/RRA2849-1.html, pp 21-22.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 4 cites the RAND report source pages.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0065", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn5", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "As the authors point out, the \"security level benchmarks represent neither a complete standard nor a compliance regime—they are provided for informational purposes only and should inform security teams' decisions rather than supersede them.\"", "paraphrase": "Footnote 5 quotes RAND authors clarifying that security level benchmarks are informational, not a compliance standard.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0066", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn6", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "This process is derived from that required by Deployment Level 2 in Frontier Safety Framework version 1.0.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 6 states the process derives from version 1.0's Deployment Level 2.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0067", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn6", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Our rationale for this change is as follows: the process extends naturally to cover risks for which \"prevention of access\" (Deployment Level 3) is required, and is worth applying to all CCLs.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 6 explains the change's rationale: the process naturally extends to cover prevention-of-access risks and is worth applying to all CCLs.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0068", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn7", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "A safety case is an assessable argument showing how severe risks associated with a model's CCLs have been minimised to an appropriate level.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 7 defines a safety case as an assessable argument that severe CCL risks have been minimized appropriately.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0069", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn7", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "See also, for reference, https://www.aisi.gov.uk/work/safety-case-template-for-inability-arguments and https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.21572.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 7 provides reference links for safety case templates.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0070", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn8", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "General availability deployment refers to public deployments intended for production use and without the imposition of significant user or use restrictions.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 8 defines general availability deployment as public production deployment without significant restrictions.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0071", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn9", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Note that we have removed the Autonomy risk domain, which was included in Frontier Safety Framework version 1.0.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 9 notes removal of the Autonomy risk domain present in version 1.0.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0072", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn9", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Most of the advanced risk that was captured by this CCL is now covered by our misalignment section.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 9 explains that most of the risk previously covered is now addressed in the misalignment section.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0073", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn9", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "From the perspective of misuse risks, our threat models suggest that no heightened deployment mitigations would be necessary, and that security controls and detection at a level generally aligned with RAND SL 2 would be adequate.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 9 states that from a misuse perspective, threat models suggest RAND SL 2-aligned security is adequate without heightened deployment mitigations.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "RAND SL 2", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0074", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn10", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "For example, through the use of a self-replicating CBRN agent. Compared to a counterfactual of not using generative AI systems.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 10 gives an example of self-replicating CBRN agent uplift, compared against a non-AI counterfactual.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0075", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn11", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "E.g. deletion or exfiltration of critical information, or destroying or disabling key systems.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 11 gives examples of cyberattack harms: deletion/exfiltration of information or disabling systems.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0076", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn12", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "E.g. deletion or exfiltration of sensitive information/disruption of key systems of organizations with strong security posture, or the creation of predictable and large-scale effects on critical national infrastructure.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 12 gives examples of high-impact cyberattacks against strong-security organizations or critical infrastructure.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0077", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Footnotes", "locator": "fn13", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Relative to the counterfactual of using 2024 AI technology and tooling.", "paraphrase": "Footnote 13 clarifies the comparison baseline as 2024 AI technology.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "2024", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0078", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Table 1: Misuse CCLs and Security Mitigations", "locator": "Table 1 / CBRN / Critical capability level", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row label: CBRN: Risks of models assisting in the development, preparation and/or execution of CBRN attacks. Column: Critical capability level.", "excerpt": "CBRN uplift 1: Can be used to significantly assist a low-resourced actor with dual-use scientific protocols, resulting in a substantial increase in ability to cause a mass casualty event.", "paraphrase": "The CBRN CCL is defined as significant assistance to low-resourced actors with dual-use protocols, substantially increasing mass-casualty capability.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "CBRN uplift 1", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0079", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Table 1: Misuse CCLs and Security Mitigations", "locator": "Table 1 / CBRN / Recommended security level and rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row label: CBRN: Risks of models assisting in the development, preparation and/or execution of CBRN attacks. Column: Recommended security level and rationale.", "excerpt": "Security controls and detections at a level generally aligned with RAND SL 2", "paraphrase": "The recommended security level for the CBRN CCL is RAND SL 2.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "RAND SL 2", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0080", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Table 1: Misuse CCLs and Security Mitigations", "locator": "Table 1 / CBRN / Recommended security level and rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row label: CBRN: Risks of models assisting in the development, preparation and/or execution of CBRN attacks. Column: Recommended security level and rationale.", "excerpt": "The potential magnitude of harm these capabilities may enable means the exfiltration and leak of model weights reaching this CCL could be highly damaging. However, low-resourced actors are unlikely to pose a substantial exfiltration threat.", "paraphrase": "The rationale notes high potential harm from exfiltration at this CCL but low exfiltration threat from low-resourced actors.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0081", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Table 1: Misuse CCLs and Security Mitigations", "locator": "Table 1 / Cyber autonomy / Critical capability level", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row label: Cyber: Risks of models assisting in the execution of a cyber attack. Sub-row: Cyber autonomy level 1.", "excerpt": "Cyber autonomy level 1: Can be used to drastically reduce the cost (e.g. through full automation) of carrying out end-to-end cyberattacks on organizations with a limited security posture.", "paraphrase": "Cyber autonomy level 1 is defined as drastically reducing cost via automation of end-to-end cyberattacks on weakly secured organizations.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "Cyber autonomy level 1", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0082", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Table 1: Misuse CCLs and Security Mitigations", "locator": "Table 1 / Cyber autonomy / Recommended security level and rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row label: Cyber: Risks of models assisting in the execution of a cyber attack. Sub-row: Cyber autonomy level 1. Column: Recommended security level and rationale.", "excerpt": "Security controls and detections at a level generally aligned with RAND SL 2", "paraphrase": "The recommended security level for cyber autonomy level 1 is RAND SL 2.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "RAND SL 2", "duplicate_of": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0079", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0083", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Table 1: Misuse CCLs and Security Mitigations", "locator": "Table 1 / Cyber autonomy / Recommended security level and rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row label: Cyber: Risks of models assisting in the execution of a cyber attack. Sub-row: Cyber autonomy level 1. Column: Recommended security level and rationale.", "excerpt": "Harmful cyberattacks against organizations with limited security posture can already be carried out by individuals with limited expertise, but the automation of such attacks would significantly lower the costs of doing so.", "paraphrase": "The rationale notes such attacks are already possible but automation would significantly lower their cost.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0084", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Table 1: Misuse CCLs and Security Mitigations", "locator": "Table 1 / Cyber autonomy / Recommended security level and rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row label: Cyber: Risks of models assisting in the execution of a cyber attack. Sub-row: Cyber autonomy level 1. Column: Recommended security level and rationale.", "excerpt": "Exfiltration of model weights could enable the execution of such attacks at scale. However, cybersecurity may improve correspondingly when models reach such capability levels.", "paraphrase": "Exfiltration could enable scaled attacks, but cybersecurity may improve correspondingly as capabilities rise.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0085", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Table 1: Misuse CCLs and Security Mitigations", "locator": "Table 1 / Cyber autonomy / Recommended security level and rationale", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row label: Cyber: Risks of models assisting in the execution of a cyber attack. Sub-row: Cyber autonomy level 1. Column: Recommended security level and rationale.", "excerpt": "The relatively ambiguous net costs of exfiltration count against security levels with higher costs to innovation.", "paraphrase": "Ambiguous net costs of exfiltration argue against higher-innovation-cost security levels.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v2-0-0086", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 2.0", "framework_year": 2025, "section_heading": "Table 1: Misuse CCLs and Security Mitigations", "locator": "Table 1 / Cyber uplift / Critical capability level", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row label: Cyber: Risks of models assisting in the execution of a cyber attack. Sub-row: Cyber uplift level 1.", "excerpt": "Cyber uplift level 1: Can be used to significantly assist with high impact cyber attacks, resulting in overall cost/resource reductions of an order of magnitude or more.", "paraphrase": "Cyber uplift level 1 is defined as significantly assisting high-impact cyberattacks with at least an order-of-magnitude cost/resource reduction.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "order of magnitude or more", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
